    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d279">

                <pb facs="0526" n="478" sameAs="frus:frus1877/pg478"/>

                <head>No. 279.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Seward to Mr. Shishkin.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1877-06-29"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 29,
                        1877</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge with thanks
                    the receipt of your note of the 23d instant, transmitting a copy of the
                    regulations to be observed by the military and civil functionaries of your
                    government during the present war in regard to the subjects of Turkey and to
                    those of the neutral states.</p>
                <p>Accept, sir, a renewed assurance of my very high consideration.</p>
                <closer><signed>F. W. SEWARD,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                        Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
